Agent SDK v2 implementation plan (codexplan)

This plan is based on:
- Specs/sdk/plan.txt (base roadmap)
- Specs/sdk/Clarification.txt (clarify.next_questions)
- Specs/sdk/Orchesrator.txt (orchestrator)
- Specs/sdk/free chat.txt (chat.free)
- Specs/sdk/full prompts.txt (all other agents/tools)

The goal is to add an OpenAI Agents SDK powered system in parallel to the current skills + flow agent system, and add a new SDK Agent tab in the UI.

---

0) Repo alignment (current code reality)
- Next.js App Router UI: src/app/
- Convex backend: convex/
- Legacy skills runner: convex/skills/* and UI in src/app/projects/[id]/agent
- Flow agent runner: convex/flow/* and UI in src/app/projects/[id]/flow-agent
- Existing tables for chat/skills: agentConversations, agentMessages, skillRuns
- No agentRuns table yet (schema.ts note at tasks.createdByRunId)

We keep legacy and flow intact and add a new sdk namespace with separate registry, prompts, and runner.

---

1) Architecture decisions (v2)
- Engine location: Convex actions (to reuse db access, existing run logging, and tool calls). If streaming becomes a requirement, add a thin Next route that proxies to Convex later.
- Separation rule: new files only under convex/sdk/* (and UI under src/app/projects/[id]/sdk-agent) so legacy can be deleted later.
- Write wall: only changeset.apply mutates DB. All other agents/tools produce intents.
- Language + JSON rules come from Specs/sdk prompts (Hebrew-first values, English keys, JSON only for tool outputs).

---

2) New SDK Agent tab (separate UI tab)
Add a brand new tab for SDK Agent so it can run autonomously without mixing with legacy or flow.

2.1 Feature flags
- Add to convex/featureFlags.ts DEFAULT_FLAGS:
  - ff_sdk_agent_tab: false (UI visibility)
  - ff_sdk_agent_backend: false (backend gating)

2.2 Navigation
- Update src/app/projects/[id]/layout.tsx to include:
  { name: 'SDK Agent', href: `/projects/${projectId}/sdk-agent`, icon: Bot }
  gated by ff_sdk_agent_tab.

2.3 New page
- Create src/app/projects/[id]/sdk-agent/page.tsx
  - Left: conversation list (reuse agentConversations)
  - Center: chat + blocks (reuse AgentChat block renderers)
  - Right: run status + approve changeset + debug
  - Buttons: Start run, Pause, Resume, Cancel, Run next, Approve changeset
  - Feature flag gate: show disabled message when ff_sdk_agent_backend is off

2.4 Data wiring
- New Convex endpoints (convex/sdk/api.ts):
  - sdk.createConversation
  - sdk.listConversations
  - sdk.listMessages
  - sdk.appendUserMessage
  - sdk.startRun / sdk.runNext / sdk.pause / sdk.resume / sdk.cancel
  - sdk.approveChangeSet

---

3) New SDK data model (telemetry)
Add new tables in convex/schema.ts to keep v2 clean and separate:
- sdkRuns
  - projectId, conversationId
  - status: running|paused|blocked|awaiting_approval|completed|failed|cancelled
  - stageKey, currentAgentName, engine='sdk'
  - parentRunId (optional for sub-agents)
  - createdAt, updatedAt, finishedAt
- sdkRunEvents
  - runId, type, payload, createdAt

Reuse agentMessages for UI blocks, and store a runId on messages for linking.

---

4) Prompt store (use Specs/sdk files directly)
Create convex/sdk/prompts.ts that embeds all prompts from Specs/sdk:
- ORCHESTRATOR_SYSTEM (from Orchesrator.txt)
- CLARIFY_SYSTEM (from Clarification.txt)
- FREE_CHAT_SYSTEM (from free chat.txt)
- FULL_PROMPTS (from full prompts.txt, split into individual tool/agent prompts)

Keep prompts in the SDK namespace, do not modify convex/skills/prompts.ts.

