5) Registry and schemas (v2)
5.1 Registry
Create convex/sdk/registry.ts with a catalog of:
- Option A agents (agentic, looping)
  - clarify.next_questions
  - chat.free
  - pricing.resolve_lines
  - procurement.shopping_plan
  - finance.ingest_receipt
  - audit.project
  - qa.print_files
  - maint.sync_and_repair
- Option B tools (single-shot, strict JSON)
  - intake.parse_brief
  - plan.elements
  - plan.tasks
  - plan.execution_phases
  - cost.build_budget
  - quote.generate
  - runbook.installation
  - ops.daily_plan
  - admin.set_labor_rates
  - admin.confirm_measurements
  - knowledge.summarize_or_update
  - changeset.compile
  - changeset.review

Each registry entry should include:
- id, kind ('agent'|'tool')
- systemPrompt
- allowedTools
- model + params
- output schema name

5.2 Schemas
- Add convex/sdk/schemas.ts with JSON schemas or Zod.
- If using Zod, add dependency "zod" to package.json.
- Validate tool outputs; if invalid, re-ask with a JSON repair prompt.

---

6) SDK tools and deterministic utilities
6.1 context.get
- Add convex/sdk/context.ts query implementing the contract from full prompts.txt:
  input: projectId, packs[], filters
  output: project, elements, tasks, materialLines, workLines, quote, runbook, knowledgeDoc, pricingCatalog, pricingLogs, recentQA
- Implement by reading existing tables and mapping to the contract.
- Keep packs minimal and only return requested sections.

6.2 knowledge.summarize_or_update
- Add convex/sdk/knowledge.ts action
- Uses Agents SDK with the knowledge prompt from full prompts.txt
- Store output in memoryDocs (kind RUNNING_MEMORY or PROJECT_CONTEXT)

6.3 changeset.compile / review / apply
- Add convex/sdk/changeset.ts
  - compile: transform intents to current changeSets ops format (kind + payload) and return a ChangeSet draft
  - review: validate structure and links (reuse existing flow validators where possible)
  - apply: call existing changeSets.applyChangeSet after explicit approval token

---

7) Agents SDK runner (core)
Create convex/sdk/runner.ts
- Use OpenAIAgent from openai-agents
- The orchestrator agent uses ORCHESTRATOR_SYSTEM and exposes tools:
  - context.get
  - knowledge.summarize_or_update
  - changeset.compile / review / apply
  - all registry agents and tools
- Implement tool dispatch so:
  - Option A agents are called as sub-agents (their own system prompt)
  - Option B tools are single-shot LLM calls with strict JSON output
- All tool outputs are validated against schemas and saved to sdkRunEvents
- Save messages as blocks into agentMessages for UI rendering

---

8) Orchestrator flow (v2)
- Stage machine per Orchesrator.txt: intake -> planning -> costing -> quote -> review -> execution
- Always pull context via context.get before planning or pricing
- Use clarify.next_questions when missing info
- Compile intents -> review -> present summary -> wait for user approval -> apply
- Never call changeset.apply without user approval

---

9) Phased build (updated from plan.txt)
Phase 1: scaffolding
- folders: convex/sdk/* and UI route
- feature flags
- schema tables sdkRuns + sdkRunEvents
- basic runner that can echo a ChatBlock

Phase 2: Option B tools
- intake.parse_brief
- plan.elements
- plan.tasks
- plan.execution_phases
- cost.build_budget
- quote.generate
- runbook.installation
- ops.daily_plan
- knowledge.summarize_or_update

Phase 3: ChangeSet chain
- compile -> review -> apply (dryRun first)
- UI approval gate in SDK Agent tab

Phase 4: Option A agents
- clarify.next_questions first
- then pricing, procurement, audit, receipt, print QA, maintenance, free chat

Phase 5: Orchestrator end-to-end
- Orchestrator can finish a full cycle on a test project
- All writes only via ChangeSet apply

Phase 6: SDK Agent tab UX
- full run controls, telemetry, approval UI
- reuse existing block components (ChatBlock, QuestionsBlock, SuggestionBlock, ChangeSetBlock, ReviewBlock, ShoppingPlanBlock, PrintQaBlock, ReceiptBlock, RunbookBlock, DailyPlanBlock)

Phase 7: Shadow mode + evaluation
- Run SDK in shadow mode against legacy/flow
- Compare elements/tasks/lines coverage, missing price rate, audit findings

Phase 8: Cutover
- Default ff_sdk_agent_tab + ff_sdk_agent_backend on for new projects
- Keep legacy and flow as fallback before removal

---

10) Acceptance criteria for SDK Agent tab
- Can start a run and see sdkRuns + sdkRunEvents + agentMessages
- Orchestrator can call at least one tool and produce valid JSON blocks
- ChangeSet dryRun compiles and review passes
- Apply requires explicit approval and updates tables correctly

---

Notes
- Keep all new code under convex/sdk and src/app/projects/[id]/sdk-agent
- Do not modify legacy skills runner or flow runner.
- Prompts must match Specs/sdk files exactly (Hebrew-first rules).
